5. Detection Methodology and Attack Coverage [18 Marks]

This is the most heavily weighted section. Detectors must decide from telemetry and
commands, not from test labels, injected-attack flags or the attack generator's state. Attacks
should include subtle cases near normal noise levels, not only large constant offsets.

