11.3 Design Integrity Declaration

We confirm that the IDS design, source code, test cases, attack scenarios, results and technical
decisions presented in this report have been reviewed and verified by the team. Every result
shown was produced by the submitted code on the data described. No detector reads
ground-truth labels or attack flags, and no result has been copied, estimated or edited to
resemble a measurement unless it is labelled as such. The team accepts responsibility for the
technical accuracy, validity and integrity of the submitted work. The evaluation committee may
request the source repository history, test logs, raw flight data, or other technical records, and
may require the team to explain, reproduce, modify or defend the technical work presented in
this report.
